I have very bad memories and fears, and probably I'm overanxious because of what happened. But you know, thank God we're alive. That's what bothers me, because I-- we lost a lot of family, mostly children, especially the ones that went to Transnistria, which was a sort of a camp, and no medication, no food. A lot of them my age died. And that was very sad, very sad. And adults and people just didn't get up in the morning because of the hardships that they had to sustain. But that's what it was. And the fact, it's very difficult to fathom that there are people that think that we made up a story.

INT: Yeah. [LAUGHING] Mhm.

